  "text": "### 4. Reporting Structure  \n**Internal Reporting:**\n- Reports functionally to Board Audit Committee (primary reporting line)\n- Reports administratively to Chief Operating Officer (for budgeting, HR, facilities)\n- Direct access to Chief Executive Officer (escalation)\n- Board Audit Committee meetings quarterly minimum  \n**External Reporting:**\n- FCA/PRA may communicate with Head of Internal Audit directly\n- Regulatory examination findings shared with Board Audit Committee\n- External audit coordination (no duplication of effort)  \n**Organizational Independence:**\n- Internal Audit separate from operational departments\n- No operational responsibilities or conflicts\n- Cannot audit areas where led/managed audit team\n- Rotates staff every 5–7 years (prevent familiarity)  \n---",
  "name": "Chunk 9/24",
